[29.016003, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[2mv0.7.4\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Provider: anthropic-vertex\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Model: claude-sonnet-4-5\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Working directory: /tmp/ami-demo-pbeUuz\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mSession: session-20261113-184329-346-0\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mPermissions: auto-allow\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mTip: Run \u001b[1mami --skill <name>\u001b[22m to pin a skill stance for the session.\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m\u2298 Indexing skipped: no project root found\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m > Create calc.py with a function `safe_divide(a, b)` that returns a/b but has a bug: it doesn't \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mhandle b=0 (raises ZeroDivisionError instead of returning None) and doesn't handle non-numeric \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255minputs. Then create test_calc.py with pytest tests covering normal division, division by zero \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m(expecting None), and non-numeric inputs (expecting None). Run the tests to show failures, fix \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255msafe_divide so all edge cases pass, rerun the tests, and print a short summary of what was fixed. \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;208m\u25b6 \u001b[39m \u001b[2m\u2234 Thinking #1\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KI'll create a buggy safe_divide function, write comprehensive tests, demonstrate the failures, fix\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[Kthe bugs, and verify the solution.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K## Step\r\r\n"]
